From: TDVP <tdvp@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: k230: arbitrate shared LS registers with CPU1 I2C4

Opt in only on the paired CPU1-vision device tree. Serialize Linux low-speed
clock RMW with the same hardware semaphore used by CPU1 and GPIO, retain
the shared APB parent, and reject Linux providers for CPU1-owned fields.
No PLL, GPU or display clock policy changes. Timeout refuses writes.
The matching RT-Smart early I2C4 clock setup is required before activation.

